# Enhanced Ansible Development Guidelines for LLM-Assisted Development

## Core Principles

- **Explicit over Implicit**: Always use fully qualified names and explicit parameters
- **Self-Documenting Code**: Write code that explains itself through clear naming and structure
- **Predictable Patterns**: Use consistent patterns that LLMs can recognize and replicate
- **Validation First**: Include validation and error handling in every significant operation

## Playbook Structure

### Required Elements

```yaml
---
# Purpose: [Clear one-line description of what this playbook does]
# Dependencies: [List any required roles, collections, or external dependencies]
# Variables: [List required variables with types and examples]
- name: "Descriptive play name that explains the business purpose"
  hosts: target_group
  gather_facts: true  # Always explicit
  become: false       # Always explicit
  vars:
    # Define all playbook-specific variables here with comments
    operation_name: "descriptive_operation_name"
    
  pre_tasks:
    - name: "Validate required variables are defined"
      ansible.builtin.assert:
        that:
          - variable_name is defined
          - variable_name | length > 0
        fail_msg: "Required variable 'variable_name' is not defined or empty"
        success_msg: "All required variables validated successfully"
      tags: [validation, always]
```

### Task Organization

- Use descriptive block names that explain business logic
- Include rescue blocks for all critical operations
- Always use `tags` for logical grouping
- Include `when` conditions explicitly rather than relying on implicit behavior

```yaml
- name: "Configure application settings"
  block:
    - name: "Update configuration file with new settings"
      ansible.builtin.template:
        src: app.conf.j2
        dest: /etc/app/app.conf
        owner: app
        group: app
        mode: '0644'
        backup: true
      notify: restart_app_service
      
  rescue:
    - name: "Log configuration failure and restore backup"
      ansible.builtin.debug:
        msg: "Configuration failed, manual intervention required"
      
    - name: "Set failure flag for monitoring"
      ansible.builtin.set_fact:
        configuration_failed: true
        
  always:
    - name: "Record operation status in log"
      ansible.builtin.lineinfile:
        path: /var/log/ansible-operations.log
        line: "{{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }} - Configuration operation completed with status: {{ 'FAILED' if configuration_failed | default(false) else 'SUCCESS' }}"
        create: true
  tags: [configuration, application]
```

## Variable Management

### Required Variable Declaration Pattern

```yaml
# At the start of every playbook/role
- name: "Validate all required variables"
  ansible.builtin.assert:
    that:
      - item.var is defined
      - item.var != ""
    fail_msg: "Required variable '{{ item.name }}' is not defined. {{ item.description }}"
  loop:
    - { var: "{{ api_token | default('') }}", name: "api_token", description: "API authentication token for service integration" }
    - { var: "{{ target_environment | default('') }}", name: "target_environment", description: "Target deployment environment (dev/staging/prod)" }
  loop_control:
    label: "{{ item.name }}"
  tags: [validation, always]
```

### Variable Documentation Template

```yaml
# vars/main.yml or playbook vars section
---
# Required Variables (must be provided by user)
# api_token: string - Authentication token for API access
# target_environment: string - Target environment (dev/staging/prod)
# application_version: string - Version to deploy (semantic version format)

# Optional Variables (with defaults)
application_name: "my-application"           # Name of the application
deployment_timeout: 300                      # Timeout in seconds for deployment operations
enable_monitoring: true                      # Whether to enable monitoring integration
backup_retention_days: 7                     # Number of days to retain backups

# Internal Variables (computed, do not override)
deployment_timestamp: "{{ ansible_date_time.epoch }}"
deployment_id: "{{ application_name }}-{{ application_version }}-{{ deployment_timestamp }}"
```

## Security and Sensitive Data

### Sensitive Operations Pattern

```yaml
- name: "Authenticate with external service"
  ansible.builtin.uri:
    url: "https://api.service.com/auth"
    method: POST
    body_format: json
    body:
      token: "{{ api_token }}"
    validate_certs: true
    timeout: 30
  register: auth_response
  no_log: true  # Prevents credential exposure in logs
  failed_when: auth_response.status != 200
  tags: [authentication, security]

- name: "Log authentication success (without credentials)"
  ansible.builtin.debug:
    msg: "Authentication successful for service integration"
  when: auth_response.status == 200
  tags: [authentication, logging]
```

## Role Development

### Role Structure Template

```
roles/
├── common/
│   ├── tasks/main.yml
│   ├── handlers/main.yml
│   ├── vars/main.yml
│   ├── defaults/main.yml
│   ├── meta/main.yml
